  "root_cause": "The parameter `queue` uses a mutable default value (a list literal). In Python, default arguments are evaluated once at function definition time, not on each call, so every call without an explicit `queue` argument shares and mutates the same list object, causing state to leak across calls.",
  "fix": "Change the signature to `def add_job(job, queue=None):` and initialize inside the body with `if queue is None: queue = []` before appending, so each call gets a fresh list instead of a shared mutable default."
}
```

